H2344.definition:
from H2342 (חוּל);
sand (as round or whirling particles)
KJV: sand.

H2345.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be warm, i.e. (by implication)
sunburnt or swarthy (blackish)
KJV: brown.

H2346.definition:
feminine active participle of an unused root apparently meaning to join;
a wall of protection
KJV: wall, walled.

H2347.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to cover, i.e. (figuratively) to compassionate
KJV: pity, regard, spare.

H2348.definition:
from an unused root meaning to cover;
a cove (as a sheltered bay)
KJV: coast (of the sea), haven, shore, (sea-) side.

H2349.definition:
from the same as H2348 (חוֹף); protection;
Chupham, an Israelite
KJV: Hupham.

H2350.definition:
patronymically from H2349 (חוּפָם);
a Chuphamite or descendant of Chupham
KJV: Huphamites.

H2351.definition:
or (shortened) חֻץ; (both forms feminine in the plural) from an unused root meaning to sever;
properly, separate by awall, i.e. outside, outdoors
KJV: abroad, field, forth, highway, more, out(-side, -ward), street, without.

H2352.definition:
